WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.801 position:73%
Gautam Adani is a self-made Indian billionaire.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.846
We've seen him buy up asset
after asset across the country.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:16.057
Ports, airports, power plants.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:20.395 position:59%
Whenever he speaks about his group,
he always says that his conglomerate's

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:23.064
goals are aligned to India's goals.

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:27.318
It is the belief in the India
growth story

00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:30.030
that keeps the Adani Group going.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.243 position:58%
As recently as just a few months ago,

00:00:35.243 --> 00:00:38.163
he was the second-richest person
in the world.

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.665
To his critics, however,
he's a more complicated figure.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:45.086
Political observers think
Gautam Adani

00:00:45.086 --> 00:00:46.963
is very close to Prime Minister
Narendra Modi.

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:50.216
This is one of the hot topics
when Narendra Modi came to power.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.931
On the morning of January 24,
about a couple of hours

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.933
after sunrise in Mumbai,

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:02.103 position:58%
journalists across
the country were greeted with a large

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:06.316
100-page document from Hindenburg
Research, in which it accused

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:10.528
this empire of essentially stock
manipulation and accounting fraud.

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:13.281 position:58%
There was an instant market reaction.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:18.745 position:63%
In Adani companies, we’re are looking at
losses of north of $130 billion.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:24.292 position:59%
The last thing Modi wants
is to be involved in any of this muck.

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:27.253 position:58%
There is no doubt that the government

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.673
of India needs empire
builders like Adani.

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:33.468
But underlying all of that,
there was a sentiment

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:37.097 position:59%
that if Adani fails,
what happens to India's own ambitions?

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.817
If you are living in

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:49.859
or visiting this country,

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:52.153
you really cannot be independent

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:53.196
of an Adani asset.

00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:57.700
Coal mined from Adani
coal mines is transported

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:02.163 position:58%
through Adani-run ports and railroads
into power plants that Adani owns.

00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:04.499
The electricity generated
from these power plants

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:09.379
then runs through Adani-owned grids
into homes built with Adani cement.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:13.216
He keeps a very, very low profile.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:17.095 position:59%
We have not seen him
splashing money, buying luxurious cars

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:20.598
or buying yachts or holidaying
in luxurious destinations.

00:02:21.891 --> 00:02:25.478
The relationship
between Adani and Modi goes back

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:29.107
decades, even before Modi
was prime minister.

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:31.901
Both of them hail from
the same state of Gujarat,

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.612 position:59%
renowned for sending out entrepreneurs
around the world.

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:38.491
Adani has grown so big, so fast.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:43.872 position:56%
Adani is aligning the business goals
of the Adani conglomerate

00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:46.583 position:59%
with the goals of Prime Minister Modi.

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:50.545
If you want to grow a country,
you need to build your airports.

00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:52.005 position:59%
You need to build your infrastructure,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.465
such as electricity grids
and power plants.

00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:58.052
It's very natural that he will lean
toward big businessmen,

00:02:58.052 --> 00:03:01.431 position:59%
big conglomerates, big business groups
to develop such kind of stuff.

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:05.310
If Modi has come to the world stage
as a political leader

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:09.564 position:59%
who understands the needs of business,
Adani has been a big contributor

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:10.857
to building this image.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.862 position:56%
There’s another level of questioning

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:19.866 position:63%
about whether Adani
is actually funding Prime Minister Modi.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.744
For instance, Prime Minister Modi,
when he was campaigning

00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:27.916 position:63%
for his first term in office,
he very publicly flew in an Adani plane.

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:30.376
The party claims that they paid

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.629
the Adani Group rent
for use of this plane.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:35.924
India's political funding
was always opaque,

00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:39.344 position:58%
but since Modi has come to power,
there's an added level of opaqueness.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.723 position:58%
The Adani Group has repeatedly denied
financial improprieties

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.475 position:63%
or receiving favors from the government.

00:03:48.811 --> 00:03:51.064
Hindenburg Research is a firm

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:54.442
incorporated in New York City.

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:58.238 position:58%
It was registered by Nathan Anderson,

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.782
who is what
we would call a short seller.

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:03.493 position:59%
He exposes discrepancies in accounting

00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:06.454 position:63%
with the intention,
of course, of driving down stock prices.

00:04:07.038 --> 00:04:09.958 position:63%
It was a very strongly worded allegation
because it said

00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:13.127
it's the biggest con in India's
corporate history.

00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:16.547
It wiped off more than $100 billion
itself.

00:04:16.547 --> 00:04:20.009
One report and a few trading
sessions has taken Gautam Adani

00:04:20.009 --> 00:04:22.804
from the top list of the world’s
richest men.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:27.767 position:61%
There were many allegations
in the Hindenburg report against Adani.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.395
The main allegation was that

00:04:30.395 --> 00:04:34.691
people close to Gautam
Adani used offshore shell companies

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:38.778
to pump up the prices of stock
in Adani's listed firms.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:42.991 position:63%
He then, according to these allegations,
used these pumped up

00:04:42.991 --> 00:04:46.494
share prices as collateral
to borrow more money from banks.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:51.082
Bloomberg has investigated
some of the funds.

00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:54.836
These are all Mauritius entities,
a country known as a tax haven

00:04:54.836 --> 00:04:59.674 position:58%
that have little or no information on
who are the beneficial owners

00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:02.760
of these funds – essentially,
where the money trail leads to.

00:05:05.096 --> 00:05:08.057
Billionaire Gautam Adani
has published a lengthy rebuttal

00:05:08.057 --> 00:05:11.019 position:61%
to allegations of fraud
by a short seller, Hindenburg Research.

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:13.313 position:58%
The report is a malicious combination

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.024
of selective misinformation, stale,

00:05:16.024 --> 00:05:18.276 position:58%
baseless and discredited allegations.

00:05:18.276 --> 00:05:22.238
The fundamentals of our company
are very strong.

00:05:22.238 --> 00:05:23.990
Our balance sheet is healthy

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.951
and assets robust.

00:05:27.869 --> 00:05:30.955 position:56%
When the Hindenburg report came out,
there were several people

00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:35.918
in India, nationalists of course
being among the forefront of these,

00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:39.797 position:59%
who said that this was just an attempt
to malign the image of India.

00:05:39.797 --> 00:05:45.303
Gautam Adani's conglomerate
saying that any attack towards

00:05:45.303 --> 00:05:49.140
Adani Group is an attack towards
India's goals.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.144
They were trying to reiterate to us
that they never defaulted

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:56.230
any payments in their history

00:05:56.230 --> 00:06:02.153 position:63%
and they always made a number
of conservative cash management tactics.

00:06:03.112 --> 00:06:07.825
So what does Hindenburg Research’s
allegation done to Adani?

00:06:07.825 --> 00:06:10.828
The aggressive expansion
has been slowed down.

00:06:10.828 --> 00:06:13.456
The capex has been slowed down.

00:06:13.456 --> 00:06:15.625 position:56%
You will not see Gautam Adani as the

00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:19.712
as the busiest dealmaker
in 2023, unlike in 2022.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:23.383 position:58%
They are continuing with this process

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:26.969
of prepaying
and repaying a whole lot of debt.

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:29.389
That seems to be a very big part

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.223
of how they're trying

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:34.018 position:63%
to portray themselves as this very
good corporate citizen, as the opposite,

00:06:34.018 --> 00:06:37.438
basically, of what Hindenburg
had alleged.

00:06:38.272 --> 00:06:40.733 position:61%
There’s good debt and there’s bad debt.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:46.030 position:61%
Of course, you have to have debt, but
what is the level of debt you can keep?

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.407
That is a key question.

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:51.911
The critical lesson
learned in this entire episode is

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:56.082 position:63%
how robust is your regulatory framework?

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:59.043 position:61%
How robust is your judiciary framework?

00:06:59.043 --> 00:07:01.796 position:56%
And how good is the Indian landscape
to do business?

00:07:01.796 --> 00:07:06.259 position:58%
As India looks to tap Western capital
more frequently,

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:10.263
it will necessarily have to adapt
to Western ways of doing business.

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:15.226 position:58%
India will have to open up
its accounting books to Western eyes.

00:07:15.226 --> 00:07:16.519
The answer to the question
of whether the

00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:20.106
Adani Group is too big
to fail is a trickier one.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:23.985
It can survive the Hindenburg
Research allegations

00:07:23.985 --> 00:07:26.946 position:56%
because it is built on strong
fundamentals and it never defaulted.

00:07:27.989 --> 00:07:31.159
Next year, Modi,
of course, has re-elections.

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:34.412 position:58%
This is something that Modi will pull

00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:37.957 position:63%
no stops to get at, his party wants that
third term in office.

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:42.503 position:69%
And, once it gets that third term in office,
Modi then needs to cement his legacy.

00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:45.965
And for that, he needs billionaires
like Gautam Adani.

